y i know this sounds kind of  weird but i kind of want some skittle to  like wash out the taste of the teddy  does that make sense  this is sparking new life in me okay i  want a few more  okay so nutrition wise  even if i wanted to kind of liven myself  up after a meal like the chicken tenders  and fries where the dominant flavor is  like i don't know  salt i would probably intuitively reach  for something fiber-rich sprightly and  refreshing so for example maybe some  really tangy juicy fruit or like crisp  vegetables and some dip but again  we know that victoria's access to  veggies in the scenario is limited so  it's super interesting to me that her  intuition said hey you know those  skittles might actually just liven up  the palette and i actually think that's  really insightful skittles have the same  tangy sweet juicy flavor that stimulates  the salvatory mechanisms in the mouth  the same way that a big bowl of juicy  tangy mango or pineapple would so even  though it's probably not going to fix  the blah feeling she's experiencing in  her belly or her energy levels since  skittles are like a naked simple carb it  may temporarily alleviate the bleh  feeling she's experiencing in her mouth  and again that is a valid need and  instinct to respond to an honor as well  she did only eat like three not the  whole bag so i wouldn't expect that  really would contribute to significantly  to her current state of black  but  if she had eaten the whole bag after her  chicken and fries it would have just  been more data for her to collect to be  like oh boy you know maybe  maybe some protein or fiber in that  snack would have felt better and maybe  would have prevented the pre-dinner kind  of  energy crash so as a gentle nutrition  tip if you're craving something like  skittles or another naked carb one great  way to honor that craving without  dipping into scarcity mentality is to  make it a hunger crushing combo so maybe  having some nuts or seeds with those  skittles would really help to stabilize  and iron out the blood sugar response so  we are back from dinner so for the  appetizer we had a caesar salad and we  had pasta i forgot to film that so this  is some footage of my um empty plate  then for dinner we had trout it was the  first time i ever had trout it came it  was delicious and then i got dessert um  i got this really delicious like three  ice cream layer cookie cake we had the  w-i-n-e okay so this meal she just  described sounds like heaven  and also pretty well balanced like we've  got some protein and healthy omega-3  rich fats in the trout we got carbs and  fiber in the pasta we got a little  veggies and also some fat in the caesar  salad and also the most epic sounding  cake i have ever heard of now is caesar  salad the most nutrient dense salad no  like there's very little fiber in  romaine lettuce compared to like a  hardier green like kale or chopped salad  that's got lots of other veggies in  there but again the girl is on vacation  and it sounds like it was an italian  restaurant so if that's what sounded  good to her or that's what was available  to her  it works i  love me a good garlicky caesar myself  now i also get the sense from watching a  lot of victoria's videos that she  doesn't eat like this every single day  so  some days i've seen her have a chicken  spinach salad other days it's nutella on  toast with berries and fruit and others  it's like a homemade chicken and rice  bowl she likely doesn't get to go out  for a ski trip with a girlfriend and  have wine and cake every day but what i  loved most about this meal is that it  sounded like the highlight was actually  the most nutrient dense part the fish  let's take a listen how are you feeling  about this day of food like oh my god  well honestly like after that trout i'm  like i never want to eat anything but  fish again  i feel amazing okay so i can't speak for  victoria but when i was struggling with  disordered eating if i had allowed  myself a meal that included cake pasta  caesar salad with full fat dressing and  wine  i probably wouldn't touch something  healthy like fish if i was in like  full-blown cheat day or binge mode i was  going to order all the foods that i  otherwise wouldn't allow myself to have  i wasn't gonna like waste space in my  stomach eating something safe and  healthy that i would just be forcing  myself to eat on the regular anyway but  you can see that with victoria and also  her friend who seems to have a really  solid healthy relationship with food as  well these women are able to appreciate  the inherent deliciousness of naturally  nourishing foods like trout that's what  happens when you stop putting like  refined carbohydrates on this forbidden  yet so alluring pedestal they just  become  another food and all foods become  morally equal and pleasure promoting and  i'm just gonna be totes honest right now  with you guys i am feeling v bloated i  posted earlier this week about being on  my period and being bloated and honestly  you guys when this happens i just really  try to embrace it like  this is my stomach this is how it is  today it's ever changing and my thought  process is just to try not to get super  obsessed and down about it but instead  just be like  well  we're bloated today okay so victoria has  given us some beautiful and truly  helpful mantras for those days when  maybe we're not feeling our best  i don't feel very good  whether it's because we over ate it's  that time of the month we've gained  legitimate weight whatever  just because you practice intuitive  eating and you aren't trying to actively  lose weight doesn't mean that you love  your body or how it looks 24 7. it would  be a complete lie if i suggested that i  never had days where i looked in the  mirror at my belly and felt  self-conscious but i have worked really  hard on the skill of body acceptance it  doesn't have to be body love but i think  that you know acceptance and respect is  a lot more attainable for most folks so  it's like saying  this is what my body looks like today  it's just a tummy it's just fat and  water and my uterus and digestive organs  how it looks doesn't depict my worth or  value and regardless of how far out my  stomach sticks it's capable of so many  amazing things including the fact for me  that has grown and housed and fed two  beautiful boys i've really had to lean  into this myself as i go through this  digestion sibo journey because there are  days when i legit look six months  pregnant again and that can be really  hard so just a reminder to try to be  kind and patient and most of all  accepting this is my body today  and it doesn't need to be changed now i  have watched a lot of victoria's channel  and i follow her closely on tik tok as  well and i have to say  that i think she is one of the most  helpful content creators out there when  it comes to rejecting diet mentality but  one of the questions i anticipate  getting from you who maybe watch some of  her videos is whether or not intuitive  eating involves what seems to be  a lot of work like  a lot of introspection a lot of  constantly checking in and asking  yourself am i hungry now am i full now  what do i crave what do i want how does  this sound how does this make me feel  etc i mean there are videos of victoria  literally walking you step by step  through her thoughts as she does  something as mundane as eating a burrito  and in one video i watched with her  boyfriend she like asks him after every  meal like how do you feel do you feel  satisfied with your choice are you  hungry still etc so is this what  intuitive eating really entails not  necessarily no as i alluded to earlier  intuitive eating isn't like other diets  that have these predetermined sets of  one-size-fits-all rules it's ultimately  a mind-body eating framework informed by  a set of principles but when you come  from a restrictive background  where you're very much used to  scrutinizing every eating episode from a  place of fear guilt or distrust you're  very likely going to need to do a lot  more of that checking in so that you can  get back in touch with your intuition  but over time the inner dialogue becomes  well  more intuitive  you've collected most of the data you  know your body and the need for more  intentional data updates are not as  constant and also like not as intrusive  i guess it's like what that calorie  counting ballerina said  it just can run in the background  except it actually can just run in the  background because you don't have to get  your scale out to weigh your corn flakes  so i do think victoria is more vocal  about her inner dialogue because she's  kind of using it as a teaching tool for  you but i doubt that this is taking up  as much mental space as it may seem it  might i mean her brain is not my brain  [Applause]  but i'm just saying that that's been my  experience anyway so if you are ready to  reject the diet mentality and are  looking for a great step-by-step  real-life tutorial on how to do it i  highly recommend checking out victoria's  content and i also hope that my  commentary on victoria's intuitive  eating commentary was helpful and  reinforcing and on that note that is all  that i have for you guys today thank you  again to squarespace for sponsoring this  video if you liked it be sure to give it  the thumbs up leave me a comment below  on who you'd like to see me review next  subscribe to the channel and i'll see  you next time on abby's kitchen bye
 

